{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018bgWdyRCXZ1jFXNuQwCHoE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd045-arch\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/arch: Print Machine Hardware Name\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  The arch utility prints the machine hardware name, equivalent to uname -m. It is used in\n6\t  scripts that branch on CPU architecture (e.g., x86_64 vs arm64) without invoking the full\n7\t  uname flag set. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (garch,\n8\t  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout and exit code, verified by differential\n9\t  testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print the machine hardware name followed by a newline.\n13\t  - G2: Reject any extra operands with an error message and nonzero exit.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default behavior\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the machine hardware name (e.g., x86_64, arm64) followed by a newline and exit 0.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: The output must be identical to guname -m on the same system.\n23\t\n24\t  R2:\n25\t    title: Error handling\n26\t    items:\n27\t      - R2.1:\n28\t          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n29\t      - R2.2:\n30\t          text: Must not accept any flags other than --help and --version. Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n31\t\n32\t  R3:\n33\t    title: Differential testing\n34\t    items:\n35\t      - R3.1:\n36\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (garch) via pkg/testutils.\n37\t      - R3.2:\n38\t          text: \"Tests must cover: normal invocation (no arguments), extra operand error, and unknown flag error.\"\n39\t      - R3.3:\n40\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n41\t\n42\tnon_goals:\n43\t  - cmd/arch does not accept any flags for selecting different information fields; use cmd/uname for that.\n44\t  - cmd/arch does not print processor type (-p) or hardware platform (-i).\n45\t\n46\tacceptance_criteria:\n47\t  - id: AC1\n48\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/arch prints the machine hardware name, matching garch.\"\n49\t    traces:\n50\t      - R1.1\n51\t      - R1.2\n52\t  - id: AC2\n53\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/arch extraarg exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching garch.\"\n54\t    traces:\n55\t      - R1.1\n56\t      - R2.1\n57\t      - R2.2\n58\t      - R3.1\n59\t      - R3.2\n60\t  - id: AC3\n61\t    criterion: \"Differential test against garch passes for normal invocation and error cases.\"\n62\t    traces:\n63\t      - R2.1\n64\t      - R2.2\n65\t      - R3.1\n66\t      - R3.2\n67\t      - R3.3\n68\t  - id: AC4\n69\t    criterion: \"cmd/arch compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n70\t    traces:\n71\t      - R1.1\n72\t      - R1.2\n73\t      - R2.1\n74\t      - R2.2\n75\t      - R3.1\n76\t      - R3.2\n77\t      - R3.3\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"acec8f0f-580e-45e5-9e80-e371a86b1d82","uuid":"87e2a2a9-da72-4c76-8fbb-07f9e2412401","timestamp":"2026-05-14T16:52:10.049Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5185/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd045-arch.yaml","content":"id: srd045-arch\ntitle: \"cmd/arch: Print Machine Hardware Name\"\n\nproblem: |\n  The arch utility prints the machine hardware name, equivalent to uname -m. It is used in\n  scripts that branch on CPU architecture (e.g., x86_64 vs arm64) without invoking the full\n  uname flag set. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (garch,\n  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout and exit code, verified by differential\n  testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the machine hardware name followed by a newline.\n  - G2: Reject any extra operands with an error message and nonzero exit.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the machine hardware name (e.g., x86_64, arm64) followed by a newline and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: The output must be identical to guname -m on the same system.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must not accept any flags other than --help and --version. Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (garch) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: normal invocation (no arguments), extra operand error, and unknown flag error.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/arch does not accept any flags for selecting different information fields; use cmd/uname for that.\n  - cmd/arch does not print processor type (-p) or hardware platform (-i).\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/arch prints the machine hardware name, matching garch.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/arch extraarg exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching garch.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against garch passes for normal invocation and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/arch compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
