{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated code generation task (task #5185) as part of the cobbler-scaffold pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The specific task is to implement `cmd/arch/main.go` - the `arch` utility that prints the machine hardware name to stdout (equivalent to `uname -m`). The task covers:\n   - srd045-arch R1.1: Print machine hardware name to stdout\n   - srd045-arch R1.2: Output formatting and newline termination\n   - srd045-arch R2.1: --help flag prints usage to stdout, exits 0\n   - srd045-arch R2.2: --version flag prints version to stdout, exits 0\n   \n   Critical constraints: No git commands, no filesystem exploration, no modifying files outside the specified list, follow execution constitution and go style constitution exactly.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `arch` coreutils utility\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binary (`garch`)\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Cannot import `golang.org/x/sys` directly in cmd/ packages - must use `pkg/sys` or Go stdlib\n   - `syscall.Uname` from Go stdlib provides machine hardware name\n   - SPDX copyright header required on all Go files\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - Write all files before building/testing\n   - No scope creep - only implement what's specified\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd045-arch.yaml` (READ)\n     - This is the full SRD for the arch utility, needed to understand exact requirements\n     - Key requirements: R1 (default behavior - print hardware name), R2 (error handling - reject extra operands/unknown flags), R3 (differential testing)\n     - Non-goals: no -p