"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/arch/main.go` with:\n     - Copyright header\n     - SIGPIPE handler installation\n     - Machine hardware name retrieval via syscall.Uname\n     - --help flag support (print usage, exit 0)\n     - --version flag support (print version, exit 0)\n     - Error handling for extra operands (stderr, exit 1)\n     - Error handling for unknown flags (stderr, exit 1)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/arch ./cmd/arch/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/arch/` to verify no issues (AC2)\n   - Verify bin/arch prints correct output (AC3)\n   - Verify bin/arch --help works (AC4)\n   - Verify bin/arch --version works (AC5)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file for arch (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd045-arch.yaml`) and was about to write the implementation of `cmd/arch/main.go`. The SRD read was the first step in the task's instruction sequence: \"Review provided context\" → \"Plan approach\" → \"Implement\" → \"Verify\". I completed the review step and was transitioning to the plan/implement step when the summary was requested.\n\n   The implementation plan:\n   - Use `syscall.Uname` to get the `Utsname.Machine` field\n   - Convert the int8 array to a Go string\n   - Print it followed by a newline\n   - Handle --help and --version with manual flag parsing (since only these two flags are accepted, and the tool must reject all other flags)\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - Handle extra operands with error message to stderr, exit 1\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/arch/main.go` implementing all four requirements (R1-R4 from the task description). The task instruction says: \"Implement -- Complete the work described in Requirements and Files to Create/Modify. Follow the Design Decisions.\" The single file to create is `cmd/arch/main.go` with the arch utility implementation. After writing, run `go build -o bin/arch ./cmd/arch/` and `go vet ./cmd/arch/` to verify acceptance criteria AC1 and AC2.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5185/acec8f0f-580e-45e5-9e80-e371a86b1d82.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"acec8f0f-580e-45e5-9e80-e371a86b1d82","uuid":"c65b88e2-5a9e-4f41-a3fa-3e4be1d9f007","timestamp":"2026-05-14T16:52:56.152Z","isSynthetic":true}
