{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R94GS5BW2s93e3LNF6sEJE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t// cmd/false exits with status 1, ignoring all arguments.\n5\t// Implements srd014-false R1.1-R1.3, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.2.\n6\tpackage main\n7\t\n8\timport (\n9\t\t\"fmt\"\n10\t\t\"os\"\n11\t\n12\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n13\t)\n14\t\n15\tconst helpText = `Usage: false [ignored command line arguments]\n16\t  or:  false OPTION\n17\tExit with a status code indicating failure.\n18\t\n19\t      --help     display this help and exit\n20\t      --version  output version information and exit\n21\t`\n22\t\n23\tconst versionText = `false (go-unix-utils) dev\n24\t`\n25\t\n26\tfunc main() {\n27\t\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n28\t\n29\t\tif len(os.Args) > 1 {\n30\t\t\tswitch os.Args[1] {\n31\t\t\tcase \"--help\":\n32\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n33\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n34\t\t\tcase \"--version\":\n35\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n36\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n37\t\t\t}\n38\t\t}\n39\t\n40\t\tos.Exit(1)\n41\t}\n42\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FPZ28N3Fbimesc67hSRaTY","session_id":"acec8f0f-580e-45e5-9e80-e371a86b1d82","uuid":"bc151286-140a-4e38-87fd-d636029557f8","timestamp":"2026-05-14T16:53:16.466Z"}
